    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mas.to/@maugendre/117520166439160595</guid>
      <link>https://mas.to/@maugendre/117520166439160595</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:23:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;New study extracts dominant influence routes from massive climate datasets. It shows causal pathways between teleconnections.&lt;br&gt;The computing framework avoids ML. Phases include:&lt;br&gt;• Gridded data is transformed and stored in relational and graph databases for fast geospatial retrieval.&lt;br&gt;• The pipeline attacks dimensionality through spatial clustering.&lt;br&gt;• Causal processing: one representative time series per cluster is computed by the SLARAC method.&lt;br&gt;• A Yen’s k-shortest path algorithm extracts the most relevant causal chains.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cruz, J. E. C., da Rocha, V. R., de Andrade, F. M., &amp;amp; Quiles, M. G. (2026). "A multivariate causal chain detection methodology assessed on the ENSO modulation of the Northeastern Brazil precipitation" &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s41060-026-01322-3" rel="nofollow noopener" translate="no" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ellipsis"&gt;doi.org/10.1007/s41060-026-013&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;22-3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/ENSO" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;ENSO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/ElNi%C3%B1o" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;ElNiño&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/causality" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;causality&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/climate" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;climate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/weather" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;weather&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/SLARAC" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;SLARAC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/networks" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;networks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/dataEngineering" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;dataEngineering&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://mas.to/tags/Brazil" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Brazil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://fosstodon.org/files/original/missing.png" type="" fileSize="" medium="image">
        <media:rating scheme="urn:simple">nonadult</media:rating>
        <media:description type="plain">Three phase approach - data transformation and ingestion (blue), clustering (green), and causal processing (orange)

from Cruz, J. E. C., da Rocha, V. R., de Andrade, F. M., &amp; Quiles, M. G. (2026). "A multivariate causal chain detection methodology assessed on the ENSO modulation of the Northeastern Brazil precipitation" https://doi.org/10.1007/s41060-026-01322-3</media:description>
      </media:content>
