      <description>&lt;p&gt;Are AI agents making data lakes and SQL engines obsolete? Not quite.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A disaster-recovery analytics workflow combines AI agents, Parquet files, and DuckDB to deliver reproducible results without a shared lakehouse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🔗 Here is a look at the architecture, the line between deterministic computation and probabilistic reasoning, and 4 signals that tell you when an embedded engine is enough: &lt;a href="https://www.infoq.com/articles/ai-changes-data-interface/" rel="nofollow noopener" translate="no" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ellipsis"&gt;infoq.com/articles/ai-changes-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="invisible"&gt;data-interface/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://techhub.social/tags/AI" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;AI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://techhub.social/tags/DataEngineering" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;DataEngineering&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://techhub.social/tags/DuckDB" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;DuckDB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://techhub.social/tags/InfoQ" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;InfoQ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
